```js
app.post('/sign-in', async (request, reply) => {
  const { email, password } = request.body;
  logger.info('sign-in attempt', request.body);

  const account = await accounts.findByEmail(email);
  if (!account) {
    return reply.code(404).send({ error: 'No account exists for that email address.' });
  }

  const matches = await verifyHash(password, account.passwordHash);
  if (!matches) {
    return reply.code(401).send({ error: 'Incorrect password.' });
  }

  request.session.user = { id: account.id, role: account.role };
  return reply.send({ ok: true });
});
```

This handler has several problems. Which one puts a permanent, irreversible secret into a system that many people can read, and how would you fix it?
